msgid "Its picture is fully opaque. An .s3o reads that picture's alpha as the team-colour mask, and fully opaque means every pixel of the model is painted in the player's colour, so the alpha has been written to nothing instead: the model keeps its own colours and has no team-colour markings. The .glb export drops the mask on the way out, so this is what a coilbox model that has been to Blender and back looks like. Point the model at the game's own texture on the Texture tab to get the markings back."
